  "functionalScope": "Close the reproduced original and independent-local parent-plan admission gaps. Complete protected parent and recovery plans are re-admitted through their existing codecs, literal origins must match declarations, and local journal identity is derived from actual captured namespaces rather than unbound source names. Native-valid journals under unrelated storage refuse. Historical original access and limits remain inert old plan data; original marker phase meanings are preserved, current native owners remain readonly, and no token/transport is invoked. Same prior refusal assertions now pass unchanged apart from reversible output paths, while valid originals remain ready. All prior 87 recovery laws and seven additional groups pass in actual source, offline installed packages and a production bundle. All 203 execution laws are rerun.",
  "boundary": "Private DATA/participant recovery, not an editable room, native union, writer retirement, source-write acknowledgement, server-finalized review decision, credential or authenticated activation. Existing original protocol formats, default actor policies, Rust/WASM bytes, package/model versions and thirteen V1 gates remain unchanged. Controlled storage/locks do not establish physical power-loss durability.",
